  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="30">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Northu">Northu</ref> 30</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-d">Gif pr<hi rend="italic">eost</hi> wið oðerne gefeohte, bete him ⁊ b<hi rend="italic">iscope</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">If a priest fights another, he is to pay compensation to him and to the bishop.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin" corresp="#wit-d">If a priest fights with another, he is to make amends to him and to the bishop.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn éin Priester gegen den andern [Priester] ficht, büsse er diesem und dem Bischofe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If one priest fights against another [priest], let him atone to him and to the bishop.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">‘⁊ b[iscope]’ was added in the 11th century.; U: checked against Whitelock, EHD I (1979), and corrected (before: ‘If a priest fights another, he is to pay compensation to him and the bishop.’).</note>
      </div>
    </body>
